TWO DIFFERENT THINGS LIVE IN THIS REPOSITORY, AND THEY ARE LICENSED DIFFERENTLY.


1. THE FORMAT AND THE CODE  —  MIT license, in full below.

   The HTML structure, the stylesheets, the scripts, the build and quality-assurance
   tooling, and the layout conventions of the Three Columns format. Take them, change
   them, build sites with them, sell what you build. That is the whole point: the
   method is published free so that the next site costs nobody anything.


2. THE WRITTEN CONTENT  —  all rights reserved.

   Copyright (c) 2026 Walter Wilkinson.

   The prose, the answers, the source previews and the reasons they are cited, the
   chronicles, the illustrations, the maps and the photographs on any page in this
   repository. These are NOT covered by the MIT grant below.

   Quoting a passage with attribution is fair use, and is welcome. Reproducing a
   page's words wholesale is not, and needs permission.


Why the split: a repository holds both a method and somebody's words. A single
permissive license at its root gives away both, including — on a real subject's site —
their price list, their insurance page and their own sentences, by a file nobody read.
The boundary is written here so that it is decided rather than inherited.


